{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/372242-dead-and-deader-vampire-and-wraith-interaction","id":372242,"title":"Dead and Deader - Vampire and Wraith Interaction","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-16T06:21:59-08:00","id":372242,"title":"Dead and Deader - Vampire and Wraith Interaction","content":"OK, so first a confession:<br /> <br /> I've never played Wraith. I've never read a Wraith book. <br /> <br /> The sum total of what I know about Wraith comes from the Kickstarter and from the White Wolf Wiki. That's it. <br /> <br /> However, I was won over enough by the above sources and some awesome people on the forums to the point where I backed Wr20 enough to be getting a physical copy of it in the future. <br /> <br /> So with that out of the way lets move on to the next point:<br /> <br /> The one game from the CWoD I know well is Vampire. Specifically Revised Edition and Dark Ages Vampire. Played in a fair few games over the years. Including the longest running campaign I've ever been in that lasted 3 years. <br /> <br /> I've been brain-storming the beginnings of a worldbuilding process that should end up with a WoD that integrates Vampire, Mage and Wraith within it bounds (all the rest are not being used, save KotE if it gets an Anniversary edition and I'll use the Masquerade version of Werewolves AKA Lupines and Demons AKA Infernal Patrons). To be clear in regards to this statement. This is not a setting where I will ever run a mixed group (well not for anything but oneshots maybe), if people are playing Vampires and dealing with Vampire issues any Wraiths run across or involved will be NPC's. Each group of supernaturals is going to be pretty much doing their own thing. However, there will be points of convergence where the actions of one group may effect the actions of another group. <br /> <br /> Ever since I backed M20 in March last year I've been thinking on and off about how Vampire and Mage might relate to one another. So things like how many shady deals the Technocracy and Camarilla might have going on, how the Order of Hermes and the Tremere might view each other and if the Chakravanti might still be hunting the Nagaraja etc. <br /> <br /> Obviously Wraith is less well known to me and I've had less time to think about points of convergence/interaction between the two groups. However, I've come up with a few ideas and I was wondering if I could get some feedback and additional ideas/hooks/possibilities from the Wraith fanbase here on the forums. <br /> <br /> I've decided to divide the thoughts I've had on this topic into two categories: General and Specific. <br /> <br /> As I don't want this post to resemble an essay I've decided to get feedback on the general points first. <br /> <br /> <b><u>General:</u></b><br /> <br /> 1) So a quote in the Revised Masquerade book (and possibly V20) in regards to Wraiths is something like:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;You'll make a few of these over the year, trust me.&quot; </i><br /> <br /> That got me thinking. <br /> <br /> If a Vampire lives long enough they are going to fuck-up and kill someone at some point. That's just the lore of averages coming into effect on a being that is predatory by nature. This means there is a chance that they will at some point create a Wraith. Obviously Vampires kill humans, sometimes out of necessity, sometimes in keeping the Masquerade, sometimes because the human is caught up in the Jyhad. <br /> <br /> The one death I want to focus on here is when a Vampire kills a human by draining them dry during a feeding session. I think this warrents a special look for a couple of reasons. Firstly, the act of feeding and the kiss is a bit of a supernatural link between the Vampire and his/her victim to start with. Which I think thematically gives a descent starting point for the Vampire being a fetter. Secondly, the act of feeding is kinda a violation and I feel is the sort of thing that's more likely to produce a Wraith then just a plain out necessity killing of some Vampires ghoul lackey. <br /> <br /> One question I have here is this:<br /> <br /> I can people killed by vampire in connection to necessity, Masquerade or Jyhad as falling under Violence for the purpose of Legion assignment (Smiling Lord right?). However, not every feeding is violent. So I am wondering what Legion those who died from Vampiric exsanguination would fall under? (Fate maybe?)<br /> <br /> 2) Moving on from that focused point. Vampire has a merit and a flaw that lets any Vampire have a bit more interaction with a Wraith. <br /> <br /> The Merit is &quot;Spirit Mentor&quot; (3pts), which is basically a Wraith that is well disposed towards the Vampire in question and helps them out. Mainly by offering advice and guidance, but also just being a person the Vampire can talk to who's not involved with the Jyhad. <br /> <br /> The Flaw is Haunted (3pts), which is having an angry Wraith follow you around and makes life difficult for you in some way. By default its a former victim of the Vampire who screws up feeding attempts most of the time. However, it's customized by the Storyteller, so it could undermine your plots, position in the city or disrupt your household. Its implied it can't directly harm you, but it can work towards your destruction. <br /> <br /> Personally I really like these particular merits and flaws. One of my previous characters picked up a Spirit Mentor in play due to some of his actions and the actions of his Sire. It added an interesting dynamic to the game. <br /> <br /> So here is the question:<br /> <br /> Do you guys think its viable to have a Vampire character take both the Merit and the Flaw and have one represent the Wraith and another the Wraiths Shadow? With the idea that the Wraith in question has trouble keeping his Shadow under control now and then. <br /> <br /> I kinda like the idea of maybe a oneshot or few session game where one PC is the Vampire and one PC is the Wraith and they kinda have a misadventure/plot together. Nice little personal story to be had in that I think. Could be played up for either fun (48 Hours), dark comedy (Withnail and I), slice of life (Being Human) or horror/thriller (Six Sense) depending on the ST and Players mood. <br /> <br /> Unfortunately, I can't really talk on the matter of Wraith merits and flaws. I don't know if there is anything similar that might help plant story seeds for interaction between Wraiths and Vampires.<br /> <br /> 3) I was thinking about the idea of a Vampire as a Wraiths fetter in the Skinlands. If that's possible at all (I'm not sure if non-objects can be fetters).<br /> <br /> So in some ways I guess it sucks. You rely on the Vampire that killed you to stay close to the Skinlands and not get sucked down into the Tempest/Sunless Sea. That's just one more injustice that the universe seems to have thrown at you. Its very likely your not going to like the Vampire in question. Yet it is kinda in your interest to keep him alive and around. This does not mean you can't cause trouble for him of course, so vengeance can be had in small amounts. <br /> <br /> However, the fact your tied to an undead being might be pretty good for you in the long run right? You've got a Fetter that's pretty much immune to mundane aging. So you don't have to worry about him &quot;breaking&quot; like a normal object or dying like a mortal anchor. Vampires are also a fair bit tougher then Humans, so the likelihood of death by accident or mundane violence is a little bit slimmer too. So you could have a way back to being close to the skinlands for centuries or millenia if your lucky.<br /> <br /> I've got no real question here, however, I am very interested in peoples thoughts in regards to this point. Do you think its possible a Wraith starts of resenting their Vampire killer but over time basically grows to kinda accept the fact that their killer is the only thing keeping them close to the world they knew? Maybe even accept that after all the loved ones and friends are dead, their killer is going to be around and forgiveness could actually occur? <br /> <br /> I'll be back later with the more specific points of Vampire that cross-over I feel. For now I must rest and think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T07:01:56-08:00","id":372494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can people killed by vampire in connection to necessity, Masquerade or Jyhad as falling under Violence for the purpose of Legion assignment (Smiling Lord right?). However, not every feeding is violent. So I am wondering what Legion those who died from Vampiric exsanguination would fall under? (Fate maybe?) </div> </div> </div>Well, it's like usual a matter of interpretation, and the debate also happens quite often between Reapers of the legions themselves, so do not worry. The Wraith could also join the Emerald Legion if killed by a Gangrel under its wolf form, or be claimed by the Beggar Lord because several factors were actually involved in his death. Yes, you could even go for the Fate legion if you want the Wraith to be involved in Underworld missions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you guys think its viable to have a Vampire character take both the Merit and the Flaw and have one represent the Wraith and another the Wraiths Shadow? With the idea that the Wraith in question has trouble keeping his Shadow under control now and then. </div> </div> </div>Yes, why not, but for me that would imply that the Wraith is closely linked to the Vampire. Something more than just being their victim (maybe a former friend/family member when both were alive?). Otherwise the Shadow wouldn't care so much about the Vampire on top of the Psyche. There's a Thorn for the Shadow ('Shadow Life', 5points) that allows her to have its own life by itself, without the Psyche even noticing it, and that Merit would totally fit here in my opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was thinking about the idea of a Vampire as a Wraiths fetter in the Skinlands. If that's possible at all (I'm not sure if non-objects can be fetters). </div> </div> </div>It is totally possible, and from the point of view of many wraiths, really useful for the reasons you mentionned. Personally I would ask my players to buy the Merit 'Vampire companion' (3 points) in order to be allowed to have such a Fetter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you think its possible a Wraith starts of resenting their Vampire killer but over time basically grows to kinda accept the fact that their killer is the only thing keeping them close to the world they knew? Maybe even accept that after all the loved ones and friends are dead, their killer is going to be around and forgiveness could actually occur? </div> </div> </div>Yes, but what you're describing here rather looks like a Wraith resolving a Fetter, i.e. losing it in terms of game mechanics and getting closer to Transcendance. If you want to tie a Wraith to a Vampire, do not forget the Passions (of the Psyche) and the Dark Passions (of the Shadow).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4701-dam","name":"Dam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4701_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T10:28:17-08:00","id":372714,"title":"","content":"If you are tying the games together at this level, you are going to need to think about how the wraith Spirit Mentor is actually doing the mentoring. Communication across the Shroud is not easy and mostly not legal from the Wraith side. So, unless the vampire is using the right Path as a Necromancer or there's a ritual in play, you will need to make sure the wraith has enough of the right Arcanoi to be able to, say, have a conversation with his Kindred buddy.<br /> <br /> In the vamp min-game I'm running right now, one of the characters has Spirit Mentor, specifically his grandfather, who has enough Phantasm that he is able to set up dreams where they can communicate. It does limit the communication in odd ways as the only thing that's enough like mortal sleep is torpor. So, if he needs to talk to grandpa or vice-versa, they have to wait until daytime to do it. (The vamp can tell his Pop-pop that he needs to talk by tagging a certain prearranged wall that happens to be near the wraith's Haunt/Pathos bar). <br /> <br /> The wraith is a former PC from a Wraith mini-game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T13:47:27-08:00","id":372858,"title":"","content":"Ok before launching into my specific points I'd like to thank Dam and Ajex for replying to the more general points that I posted up a few hours ago. Due to the size of this post I\u2019ve divided it in half (making it three posts total now rather than two).<br /> <br /> <b><u>Specific:</u></b><br /> <br /> Necromancy:-<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve divided them up by Path\u2019s that actually interact with Wraiths as I\u2019ve not got the energy to list every single ritual. However, ask a pre-emptive question:<br /> <br /> Do Wraiths have a particular stereotype about Necromancers within Stygian culture? So are they culturally loaded to be wary of them, scared of them or more open to deal making with them?<br /> <br /> Most of the below is just my observations and thoughts about how different Necromancy Paths might effect a relationship between a Wraith and Vampire. At some points I post questions, but really I am more looking for other people\u2019s take/ideas/thoughts on how these powers might change a Vampire/Wraith dynamic.<br /> <br /> The Path of Bone \u2013<br /> <br /> So most of this path is not really directly going to relate to Wraiths except the Level 4 and 5 powers.<br /> <br /> Level 4 is a pretty horrific way of getting to interact with your loved ones again as a Wraith, since they temporarily pop over to your side of the Shroud while under the effect of this power. It\u2019s pretty drastic, but its an option for desperate or amoral Wraiths who have a Necromancer ally.<br /> <br /> Level 5 is of course a massive bargaining chip for a Necromancer. As its basically (as written) gives the Wraith a second shot at life in a mortal body. Sure it\u2019s not the Wraiths original body, but he get to live a life again. Though who knows what his Shadow might get up to in the world of flesh?<br /> <br /> The Path of the Cenotaph \u2013<br /> <br /> Lots of good stuff here, mainly for the Necromancer to get one up on a Wraith, but more altruistic uses can be seen.<br /> <br /> Level 2 lets you see fetters which is pretty useful for any Necromancer who is trying to bargain with a Wraith.<br /> <br /> Level 3 helps find weakpoints in the Shroud. Handy for working out the best places for a Wraith to attempt to influence the Skinlands.<br /> <br /> Level 4 lets you find new Wraiths as people die. Surely a boon to anyone doing an Reaping?<br /> <br /> Level 5 allows the Necromancer to make \u201cfake\u201d fetters for the Wraith. While they are only temporary, the ability to keep having fetters in the Skinlands and therefore stay near the living is a pretty hefty favour to grant.<br /> <br /> The Path of Haunting \u2013<br /> <br /> This whole Path is great for leveraging Wraiths at two levels.<br /> <br /> Firstly, it\u2019s very useful as a way of tormenting people the Wraith might want vengeance on in general. This is particularly true of the Level 5 power, which could be fluffed as the Wraith ally gaining easier access to the victim rather than a random group of Specters.<br /> <br /> Secondly, it\u2019s a great tool to threaten the Wraiths loved ones with. As Level 4 is basically putting a mortal through a harrowing (something now Wraith would wish on person they cared about). Level 5 draws Specter attention to said loved ones. Another thing most Wraiths could not conscience having done to someone they cared about.<br /> <br /> The Path of Sepulchre \u2013<br /> <br /> Level 2\u2019s uses are obvious. It lets you summon a Wraith, even one who is sucked down into the Sunless Sea. That\u2019s pretty useful for making sure a Wraith never escapes you and as a \u201crescue operation\u201d to drag an allied Wraith back if they get banished there.<br /> <br /> Level 4 is a bit like the Level 5 Cenotaph Path. Except it grants less freedom to the Wraith, goes give it a Fetter to stay out of the deeper Underworld though. So it might actually be done more benign reasons then it might first appear.<br /> <br /> Level\u2019s 3 and 5 are both gross interaction powers. Basically Dominate on Wraiths and an ability perfect anti-Wraith physical attack. I\u2019d put both in the \u201cpurely antagonistic\u201d category. That being said, its handy to have a Necromancer ally who can pull this off the Wraith\u2019s ghostly enemies. Gives a bit more of an immediate tool for the Necromancers use in a more Wraith focused game. Though the question is if a Wraith would ever actually trust a Necromancer that has these powers?<br /> <br /> The Path of Ash \u2013<br /> <br /> Probably the best set of Necromantic powers for a straight Vampire/Wraith crossover game. As it lets you interact with not only Wraiths but the Underworld more directly.<br /> <br /> Level 2 is talk with Wraiths, which I presume is something any materialized (as in on our side of the shroud) Wraith can do? So the power is useful for allowing cross-shroud communication.<br /> <br /> Level 3 allows you to hold onto ghostly objects, meaning you can keep hold of relics and such for your Wraith ally. Alternatively, it might allow you to steal said relics and then use them as a bargaining chip with more adversarial Wraiths.<br /> <br /> Level 4 is the power you want to have adventures with your Wraith ally in the Underworld. Though you going to need to bring a load of blood with you. The number of ways this helps about a Vampire/Wraith game are huge, so I\u2019m not going to try and list them here.<br /> <br /> Level 5 makes it much easier or harder for a Wraith to interact with the living world. It\u2019s easy to see the bargaining value of this ability. Not only for those Wraiths that want to interact with former loved ones (and will do what the Necromancer wants if they ever want to be able to do so again, in a more cut-throat relationship between the two parties), but for Stygian official\u2019s who want to prevent interaction between Wraiths and the living.<br /> <br /> The Vitreous Path \u2013<br /> <br /> Level 3 is where this one gets interesting. Being able to absorb the energy of entropy itself (Oblivion taint anyone) or eat ghosts like they were mortals. Obviously, the latter ability allows for the Necromancer to survive in the Underworld without having to carry around a load of blood, which is useful for crossover games.<br /> <br /> Still considering soulmarks and all that, I imagine someone who is using this ability likely looks pretty dodgy to Wraiths.<br /> <br /> Level 4 makes mortals, Vampires and Wraiths look like they are tainted by Oblivion, which is pretty bad for their social standing. Plus a fantastic tool for setting up rivals for a fall. Do you think it\u2019s possible that this power might even temporarily strengthen a Wraith\u2019s Shadow?<br /> <br /> The other ability here is to summon a small group of Specters to cause havoc for possibly miles around. However, it\u2019s not all bad as the Necromancer does not control them directly (unless he/she has Compel Soul) and they can\u2019t sense the Necromancer to trouble him/her (save for a botch).<br /> <br /> I imagine this is a risky prospect with a Wraith around (and for the Wraith who is around the Necromancer) but I could see it being used as a distraction or weapon of last resort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","user":"Hawthorn","date":". 01-16-2015, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T09:18:11-08:00","id":373525,"title":"","content":"Ok so for the third part of this brainstorming process. As before, I\u2019ve got a few questions below. Most of its ideas/thoughts/hooks I could think of with my limited knowledge of Wraith. Once again, anyone with a better grasp of that game should feel free to chip in with ideas here.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m focusing on the various Clans and Bloodlines that deal with Wraiths. I have no idea if any of them receive any coverage in the Wraith books. If there is a cannon Wraith perspective on these groups of Vampires, I would be interested in them. <br /> <br /> <u>Specific:</u><br /> <br /> 1) The Giovanni:<br /> <br /> This is the big one as they say. I'd like to state for the record I'm not really a fan of the Giovanni. They are a little dry in their fluff for me. Plus I have never really loved the taboo necromantic mafia thing. However, I do know their fluff reasonable well.<br /> <br /> Seems to me they are pretty much jerks to Wraiths. They treat them like a resource rather then as individual people. They want to catch 1 Billion Wraiths and use them to enact some massive Necromantic ritual to become Death-Gods. Which may or may not involve sundering the Shroud as well.<br /> <br /> So...with what little knowledge I have of Wraith, am I the only one that thinks their being taken for a ride by some powerful force in the Underworld?<br /> <br /> As a follow up question: Does Wraith detail how Oblivion corrupts other supernaturals? I know Mages get a build up of death resonance called Jhor, which sounds like Oblivion taint to me (does Wraith talk about that at all?). I've never seen anything in any Vampire book's that deal with Necromancy talk about Vampires getting corrupted by Oblivion though. So I was wondering if Wraith addresses this issue.<br /> <br /> 2) The Cappadocians:<br /> <br /> So the Cappadocians were a lot less involved with Wraiths according to the fluff. Since they focused on the more material aspects of death and entropy. Though the new V20DA makes that a little less clear and implies the Cappadocians did have some dealings with Wraiths before the Giovanni showed up. <br /> <br /> However, the Harbingers of Skulls (the survivors of the Giovanni purge) did hang out in the Underworld for around 600 years. So I imagine they must have kicked at least one Dark Kingdom during that time (likely Stygia). During that time they likely had to cut some deals with at least one faction of Wraiths to survive.<br /> <br /> I was wondering if anyone had any idea what group within Stygian society would be most likely to ally with or &quot;look after&quot; a group of powerful Necromancers who were physically in the Underworld (rather then being the Wraith of a Mage for example) and were all low generation elder Kindred?<br /> <br /> 3) The Samedi: <br /> <br /> These guys are based in the Caribbean. They practice Voudoun Necromancy and seem to be the favoured Kindred (unlike the Serpents of Light who he kinda trolls and who also practice Voudoun Necromancy) of the Loa Baron Samedi (which is also the name of the Bloodline founder). Necromancy is not as wide spread among them as it was for the Cappadocians nor the Giovanni in the modern day. However, they are probably the most notable &quot;new world&quot; necromancers in Masquerade.<br /> <br /> So even a relative Wraith layman like myself can see a link between the Samedi and Les Invisibles. Especially considering the latter's close ties with mortals. This might cause conflict, as Wraiths of Les Invisibles might not appreciate Samedi feeding on their still living relatives. However, the Les Mysteres beings that Les Invisibles serve could easily be the same Loa entities the Samedi pay homage too. So the two might groups of supernatural might be working towards the same ends. <br /> <br /> I can see a lot of potential for cross-over with these two groups just on face value. However, I am curious to know more about Les Invisibles and their masters before I am completely sold on the idea. That being said, I have no real question on this one, save that I am interested in hearing other peoples take on possible relationships between the two groups.<br /> <br /> 4) The True Black Hand/The Nagaraja:<br /> <br /> So Enoch is a city in the Sunless Sea right? A sort of mini-Dark Kingdom all of its own. Lorded over by the True Black Hand, which calls Vampires, Mages and odder things its members. I vaguely remember it being stated some old and powerful Wraiths also worked for/with the True Black Hand as well.<br /> <br /> As such I have the following question:<br /> <br /> How well known about is Enoch in the various Dark Kingdoms?<br /> <br /> Are the True Black Hand as stealthy and removed from events as they are in the material world? Always guiding but never showing their presence? What sort of thing in Stygian/Underworld politics might they want to influence? Considering they try to bring order to the world, but also drive it towards its end.<br /> <br /> Also, considering the metaphysics of the Underworld and Wraith, it seems sorta likely that the Aralu the Black Hand worship/serve are Neverborn (or powerful Onceborn maybe). Anyone thought on that one?<br /> <br /> The Nagaraja have a great ability to control Wraiths, but also alone among Kindred Necromancers can use Oblivion as a power-source. Controlling Specters, causing entropic breakdown of substances and even being able to feed off Wraiths as if they had blood points.<br /> <br /> Considering all this, are they sorta seen as &quot;boogeymen&quot; among the Wraiths that know about them (which I imagine is a small number)? I mean if any group of Kindred is corrupted by Oblivion its the Nagaraja. <br /> <br /> Do you thinks its plausible, given the Nagaraja's attention towards the study of Oblivion and the True Black Hand being a Gehenna cult that they might work with as well as against Specter forces in the Tempest? Perhaps pitting different Onceborn against one another but at the same time helping them take down other factions that indirectly oppose the True Black Hand in the Underworld? Maybe the True Black Hand even has Specter Cults in it, would that be viable?<br /> <br /> 5) The Rest:<br /> <br /> So off the top of my head there are three others groups of Kindred that involve themselves with Wraiths:<br /> <br /> - The Serpents of Light<br /> Pretty much fall into the same sorta relationship as the Samedi, except much less likely to be on friendly terms I feel as the Loa don't seem to like them much. So likely a more tense/antagonistic relationship at least.<br /> <br /> - The Setites <br /> Setite Sorcerers have the option of learning a few powers that interact with Ghosts. Most of these are focused on the Egyptian dead though. So I imagine that's involved with the Dark Kingdom of Sand in the Far Shores and likely beyond the purview of most Wraiths. Still, could bring about some on/off again conflict with the Ferrymen due to their relationship with Anubis.<br /> <br /> - The Impundulu<br /> The new Laibon bloodline from V20DA. These guys like to hunt down comparative magics of all types and in particular other Necromantic magics. So I don't think its too much of a stretch that they are likely interested in the study of Wraithly abilities as well. They are already pretty well primed for Crossover with their bloodline weakness and fluff tying them to a Life Sorcerer/Mage. I can imagine a relationship between them and the Dark Kingdom of Ivory as similar in its variability to the one between the Samedi and Les Invisibles. Some Impundulu might be on good terms thanks to proper ancestor worship and respect for the Old Gods. Other's might be on bad terms due to misuses of their power.<br /> <br /> In regard to these three factions I've not really got any questions. Once again, I've just stated by suppositions in regards to them. I am interested in the ideas and thoughts of people who know Wraith better in regards to these groups however. Obviously I know this requires a bit of knowledge about Masquerade as well, but I'm interested in the Wraith point of view primarily. <br /> <br /> Anyway, thanks for trudging through this essay to provide me with some answers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T10:19:44-08:00","id":373583,"title":"","content":"1) No Wraith likes the Giovanni. They are the ones warned about. Remember that the Puppeteers keep a somewhat close eye on Vampires as they tend to educate those about to Rise of them so that they could masquerade as one and their general advice is to just avoid them. Also they tend to remind their own of the fact that Possessing Vampires has the slight disadvantage that if you pick a poor host you might accidentally awaken some ancient Necromancer that the host had Diablerized and then your in trouble, so avoiding Diablerists is recommendable and the Giovanni are not only the most well known Vampires able to do anything against Wraiths but they are also Diablerists who ate the last Clan of Death so all in all bad news.<br /> <br /> Of course not all Giovanni are necessarily complete bastards and some do realize that you get more honey with sugar than vinegar but they do tend to see things as a master/slave relationship non-the-less even if they won't necessarily show it to the slave.<br /> <br /> So bottom line Wraiths do not in general trust Necromancers, after all they are practically the only ones within the Skinlands to have advantage over the dead usually the shoe is firmly on the other foot. Remember though that the important distinction is that while Wraiths tend to react with fear, resentment and anger to Necromancy they are usually extremely interested in any Mediums or those who can see/hear them thanks to some quirk or another, so those with the Merit that allows you to sense spirits nearby can be rather liked even.<br /> <br /> There is plenty of mentions of the Giovanni in Mediums if I recall correctly and in general in the opinions about Vampires.<br /> <br /> Wraith doesn't really detail Oblivions touch upon the other supernaturals. But Mediums does have rules for Spectre Cults including Investments that Spectres can grant the living. I would expect those Investments to work similarly with a supernatural recipient as well but such deals are usually easier to make with clueless mortals than the supernatural. There are mentions of Oblivion taint here and there though, mostly I would probably look at Dark Reflection Spectres (and possibly Doomslayers Into the Labyrinth) where it details how and what Spectres see most clearly in the Skinlands (as for them the Shroud is effectively thicker and they only see clearly those tainted by Oblivion) but the Giovanni have a habit of trying to find Conduits left behind from destroyed Risen which are filled with bad mojo, Oblivion taint and tend to lower the Shroud around them all in all those warehouses are twisted places.<br /> <br /> I can see if I have time to check Mediums for that Oblivion Taint thing and Spectral Investments on supernaturals but I can't make any promises as the timing is rather poor and I'm about to go away from my precious books for the next week.<br /> <br /> 2) Cappadocians. Wraith never got it's own DA supplement so there really isn't much about these guys. After all Wraith was written at a time when Necromancy was it's own very distinct Discipline and Mortis was it's own thing, so Cappadocians didn't really have much to go on with Wraiths and like said at the time of Wraith they were already long gone. Still there are those mentions of old Necromancers that the other Vampires have eaten so...<br /> <br /> Harbingers of Skulls suffer from similar malady as they were basically conceived well after Wraith had it's run. So there isn't much about them.<br /> <br /> 3) Samedi. Of them there are a few mentions, this is the time they still had Clan Disciplines of Obfuscate, Necromancy and Thanatosis (and the Kiasyd had the triple whammy of Obteneration, Mytheceria and Necromancy. What can I say, 2nd edition?) after all but I cannot recall any specifics other than perhaps an advice to avoid those that look like walking corpses, this actually might affect the Harbingers as well. Again my memory is a bit shoddy here but I'll try to find some time to check a few sources.<br /> <br /> 4) The location of Enoch, and it's existence as a Vampire city in general, was pretty much only know to few Ferrymen perhaps along side Anubis. It was one well kept secret but then again Tempest being what it is it's not entirely surprising though I would wager that few Spectres know of the place as they have amongst them some rather seasoned travelers and the information can potentially move fast through the Hive Mind. As for the Aralu... there has to be a reason the Spectres have allowed it to float there...<br /> <br /> But the Nagaraja are a small line and they tend to hang in Enoch which is practically unknown to most so for those who have heard of them they really are the proverbial boogeymen. Such rarities are not even necessarily associated with Vampires but perhaps some rare plasmics or other odd creatures found in the Tempest.<br /> <br /> 5) These are all a bit after Wraiths run so there is little to no official data on them.<br /> <br /> Setites have since time immemorial been at war with the Shemsu-heru and thus likely to have bad reputation on both sides of the Shroud in Egypt, and that their Sorcery basically involves ritualistic defilement of mummified corpses and other such things that could be powerful Fetters to some rather old and powerful Wraiths does not really help the matter.<br /> <br /> The Imbundulu are completely new invention of the new DA line so I have nothing really to say about them other than they are Necromancers and with their knowledge of the Cenotaph Path and thus ability to find Fetters they likely are not well liked. I could have more pleasant things to say about the lines presented in KotEK since there is a clear respect for ancestors present throughout the Laibon Legacies but since that book was decided to cast aside here there is practically nothing to lean on here.<br /> <br /> Hopefully this is of some help even if it is reliant on my decaying memory but like said I'll try to find time to hit the books though I wouldn't hold my breath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T23:23:15-08:00","id":374084,"title":"","content":"Checked Mediums and like I remembered there is a 6 pages devoted to the Giovanni,p.84-90, also like I remembered the Giovanni are not spoken of in the most amiable of terms.<br /> <br /> It also mentioned the following:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> Mediums p.84</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though members of other, more esoteric bloodlines possess the means to contact wraiths (the Kiasyd, Samedi and Nagaraja also use the Discipline of Necromancy), there are hardly enough of these vampires around to field a softball team, let alone pose a serious threat to the myriad denizens of the Shadowlands.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that is about all they have on those bloodlines.<br /> <br /> As a side note one notable thing is that Potchli and his ilk have much more amiable relations with the local wraiths than the Giovanni at large do but the Pisanob are still Giovanni and so the relations are strained to say the least.<br /> <br /> The Harbingers do have a small chapter of their own, p.88, but they are only spoken of as solitary mysteries with Necromantic powers that seem to be of different nature than those wielded by the Giovanni.<br /> <br /> The Spectre cult chapter does not mention if they can give investments to the supernatural but the taint of Oblivion is quite clear in those cults and includes mental, physical and social side effects resulting from the Spectres presence. a Thing to note is that most Spectral Investments are temporary, as Spectres do not wish to expend themselves to create more permanent versions though they are capable of doing so it is merely costly, but extremely dangerous for the recipient non the less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T23:55:00-08:00","id":374944,"title":"","content":"Right, this is the surprise extra round stuff I was thinking of while writing up all the other points from the other posts. Hence its late addition, honestly though, it\u2019s the last bit of my brainstorming process.<br /> <br /> The Metaplot Stuff \u2013<br /> <br /> So I\u2019ve been looking through the Noddist/Clan Lore for a lot of the Clans. It seems there is a fair bit of potential for different Antideluvians to have had at least some interaction with the Underworld and Wraiths. I\u2019ve listed the ones I feel might have some relevance to both Wraith and Vampire.<br /> <br /> Obviously this is not the sort of thing your average PC is going to find out or interact with, but I think it\u2019s important for setting background and world building.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Antediluvians:</u></b><br /> <br /> <u><i>Cappadocius -</i></u><br /> <br /> According to the Gehenna book Cappadocius pulled a fast one on Giovanni and ended up in the Underworld looking for a way to God (to eat him\u2026Ashur was a little crazy). He\u2019s either a Wraith or a sorta Astral/Soul Projection with access to all his powers (because he\u2019s an AntiD and they kinda break the rules for most Disciplines anyway). He\u2019s at least 9000 years old when he entered the Underworld not to mention the most powerful Necromancer on the planet.<br /> <br /> If I remember correctly he sources mention he was hanging around in the Labyrinth of all places for most of his nearly 600 year stay in the Underworld. So it\u2019s not likely he had that much interaction with most of Wraith society (because only a few of them are crazy enough to go down there). Frighteningly I guess it\u2019s more likely he\u2019s been \u201cpicking the brains\u201d of the Specters down there and maybe trying to glean some method of eating God from the hive-mind of Oblivion.<br /> <br /> Still a being of this magnitude of power is likely to have some impact right? I mean someone had to notice. Sure likely a lot of them went <b><i>\u201cLet\u2019s stay the hell away from that thing.\u201d </i></b>but it\u2019s still an interesting point. You can\u2019t really just ignore something that powerful, because it has the potential to screw up all our carefully laid plans. <br /> <br /> <u><i>Augustus Giovanni \u2013</i></u><br /> <br /> Cappadocius is opposite number and would-be replacement among the Third Generation. He\u2019s the youngest and weakest of the Antediluvians. However, he\u2019s a frighteningly powerful Necromancer and still a massively powerful Vampire.<br /> <br /> Some of the fluff indicates that he knows Cappadocius\u2019s soul got away from him and that despite his best efforts he can\u2019t locate an item suitable enough to try and Summon his old Sire\u2019s soul to him. As such he has made some efforts (usually through Wraith proxies/slaves to Clan Giovanni and his own childer) to find Cappadocius in the Underworld. He\u2019s not been successful as of yet.<br /> <br /> The tie in between Augustus looking for Cappadocius and Cappadocius kinda-sorta-not really hiding from him is an obvious plot link.<br /> <br /> Other stuff that can be said for Augustus is that he is quite active for an AntiD and does enjoy a good bit of politic when he can. However, the fact that he\u2019s the mastermind behind the \u201ccapture a billion ghosts\u201d plan likely means most of his interactions are pretty hostile towards the Dark Kingdoms.<br /> <br /> Do you people think it\u2019s possible for Augustus and his Clan to have a less antagonistic relationship with a Dark Kingdom? Otherwise he comes off as a bit of a Necromancer boogyman wanting to kidnap every Wraith that comes near his Clan.<br /> <br /> <u><i>Set \u2013</i></u><br /> <br /> So the Gehenna book states he\u2019s physically kicking around the Underworld (though it never explains exactly how he got there, or how he survived the Sixth Great Maelstrom when Cappadocius does not) and waging a conflict with \u201cThe Western Lands\u201d there. One could also ask the question of what he\u2019s feeding off down there, but once again he\u2019s an AntiD, so let\u2019s not dwell on that too much (it\u2019s implied his Lector Priests keep him fed on Setite faith anyway). <br /> <br /> This sounds to me like he\u2019s trying to either take over a Far Shore realm, or he\u2019s at war with the Dark Kingdom of Sand. Considering they are allies with the Ferrymen, this likely means he\u2019s in conflict with the Boatmen too.<br /> <br /> Now, the Ferrymen are all mysterious obviously and the Dark Kingdom of Sand is one of the best hidden places in the Underworld, so it\u2019s unlikely this particular conflict has drawn much attention. Surely though this will affect how Wraiths might actually get to the Dark Kingdom of Sand though? Or at least be used to explain why the Ferrymen are so busy most of the time.<br /> <br /> You could also bounce off the question of where Set is getting the forces to attack said Far Shore or Dark Kingdom? I mean he\u2019s a frightening powerful Vampire for sure, but he\u2019s up against an entire Pantheon of Gods, their Wraithly followers and the Ferrymen. Seems he\u2019d likely need some help right? Considering how some people link him to the Wyrm, its possible he\u2019s able to draw help from Specters and other creatures of Oblivion. <br /> <br /> <u><i>Arikel \u2013</i></u><br /> <br /> One story (though not the cannon one according to the Gehenna book) holds that Set killed Arikel during the time of the Second City. Considering he ate her heart in this tale. It\u2019s possible such a gruesome death might have left her as a Wraith.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s add to this that another name she goes by is Ishtar, famous for travelling to the Underworld and trying to get a loved one back to the land of the living. <br /> <br /> If she did become a Wraith she\u2019s likely one of the oldest ones in the Underworld (presuming that she\u2019s not been destroyed by Oblivion. So she could be a mover and shaker in any one of the Dark Kingdoms (though Stygia is most likely\u2026not including Enoch of course, if we consider her Wraith/Specter as a possible member of the Aralu) under another name. Alternatively, if her Shadow won out, she would be a good candidate for one of the Onceborn maybe?<br /> <br /> <u><i>Ventru \u2013</i></u><br /> <br /> Unlike Arikel, the cannon version of Ventru\u2019s story has him die (by Troiles hand) outside the gates of the Second City shortly before the city fell. Some evidence exists that he planned his own death and might have even be suicidal. So like the non-cannon Arikel, there is a descent candidate for him to become a Wraith.<br /> <br /> Like non-cannon Arikel, this would make him one of the oldest and most powerful Wraiths in the Underworld (presuming he survived once again). It\u2019s hard to imagine him not getting involved with Wraith society on some level. The jury is out on if he ever really enjoyed leadership roles and politics, but he was certainly very good at those things. <br /> <br /> From what I roughly know he makes a pretty good candidate possibly for the Quiet Lord (who is pretty mysterious in cannon even before we try and crossover fluff gymnastics) of Stygia I think. Not sure how else he could work. Possibly as one of the First among the Ferrymen, that would be kinda awesome as well.<br /> <br /> <u><b> Other Entities: </b></u><br /> <br /> <u><i>Abel \u2013</i></u><br /> <br /> He\u2019s the first human to ever die and the first murder victim. It seems pretty thematically appropriate that he becomes a Wraith to me. Hell, he\u2019d technically be the first Wraith.<br /> One Gehenna scenario even has the PC\u2019s call up Abel as a Ghost to confront Caine. So it seems to fit that he\u2019s still around and not Shadow-Eaten by the modern nights.<br /> <br /> One thought that springs to mind and keeps him in the same line as Ventru above is that as the first person to die from violence he\u2019d be the default choice for the first (not the later backstabbing one) Smiling Lord position (if he got involved with the Stygian experiment under Charon).<br /> <br /> Alternatively, a nice little twist could be that he did become Shadow-Eaten and his Shadow started off the whole manifestation of Oblivion in the Underworld. Maybe he\u2019s now a stupidly powerful Onceborn or even the entity sitting at the heart of the Void.<br /> <br /> There is always the Ferryman option as well. Alternatively he might be a Shining One on one of the Far Shores. I feel he\u2019s unlikely to transcend until his business/issues with Caine are resolved.<br /> <br /> <u><i>Eve \u2013</i></u><br /> <br /> So she\u2019s the Lady of Fate right?<br /> <br /> Seems she has enough metaplot ties as it is. Don\u2019t really need to come up with more for her really.<br /> <br /> Though I imagine if Abel is a presence in the Underworld, she has some sort of relationship with him. This relationship could take any number of forms depending on the state/status of Abel obviously. I feel it\u2019s an interesting idea she\u2019d have him to keep an eye on Charon/The Deathlords if we go with first theory.<br /> <br /> Also am I the only one that wonders what would happen if the Lady of Fate and Lilith ran into each other again? As Eve still seems to want to forgive Caine, while Lilith wants revenge on him. Though beyond the way both of them relate to Caine they both have their own history to work out. <br /> <br /> <u><i>The Neverborn \u2013</i></u><br /> <br /> So the Neverborn in Wraith are entities that predate our realities existence. Existing in this reality is torment to them and they hate every aspect of our reality. They want everything to cease so that they can go back to non-existence (as we understand it) which seems to be their natural habitat. If they ever woke up they would pretty much start demolishing our reality in short order. Luckily they spend most of their time asleep because the Underworld, while less painful to them then the living one, kinda dopes them up a fair bit.<br /> <br /> So the Children from Clanbook Baali are entities that predate our realities existence. Existing in this reality is torment to them and they hate every aspect of our reality. They want everything to cease so that they can go back to non-existence (as we understand it) which seems to be their natural habitat. If they ever woke up they would pretty much start demolishing our reality in short order. Luckily the Baali use atrocities and the \u201cbreaking\u201d of their True names to keep them asleep in the hidden and deep \u201cplaces\u201d of the living material world.<br /> <br /> Hang on a second\u2026<br /> <br /> If we tie this in with the story at the start of the Baali Clanbook that some of the Children burned up and died when God created the light at the start of time, well, it seems the Neverborn might be \u201cdead\u201d (I use this term loosely, I don\u2019t thinking something that pre-dates our reality can really die as we understand the concept at least) Children.<br /> <br /> Anybody else had this thought? Anyone come up with other possible links between Vampire stuff and the Neverborn? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T07:17:22-08:00","id":375240,"title":"","content":"I think that Abel appears in the last Orpheus book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T10:49:39-08:00","id":375378,"title":"","content":"Yeah, one of the ways that Grandmother can be stopped in the end of Orpheus, WtO's spiritual successor, is to locate a specific one of her Memory Towers, inside the PCs discover a ghost chained to the tower. He's the ghost, or perhaps the memory, of the first murder victim and wraith and because of his nature could shunt a great deal of energy from the living world into Grandmother, rendering her dormant once again. Though to get the amount of energy required to do that you have to sacrifice a great deal of life, the examples being given include the Brazilian Rainforest or a larger city.<br /> <br /> As for Abel being a better choice for the position of the Smiling Lord, well here's the thing the Hierarchy wasn't the original political body of the Dark Kingdom of Iron. Much like the Roman Empire, it was a Republic with more of a focus on protecting the dead so they could resolve their unfinished business and move on. There were legions back then but it doesn't sound like they were the Legions as they are now. Back then they were just that, the military force of the Stygia that protected the dead from the forces of Oblivion. And the position of Deathlord didn't even exist. It was after the First Great Maelstrom hit the Underworld that Charon turned the Republic into an Empire. the legions and senate of the dead were folded together with the first Deathlords* largely all being form senators in the Republic, presumably ones that represented wraiths that died along those lines.<br /> <br /> Charon himself was a Mesopotamian wraith, making him much younger than Abel, the Second City and the Flood. So if they really wanted to include Abel in the Hierarchy it would make more sense for him, as the First Murder Victim and Wraith to be in Charon's position than as the Smiling Lord. However I feel that would ultimately not be as great. Caine, Abel, Lilith and Eve are all presented as these very enigmatic. In <i>Gehenna</i>, Caine only features in one of its scenarios, the rest he's either not present or off in the far background of things. Having Abel involved with WtO would have hurt things as Charon is a major player in WtO and his more humble origins, free of the other lines helps that. Having Abel-as-Charon would have tied it to VtM and demanded that there be some ultimate connection between the two lines for its end.<br /> <br /> As for Eve and the Lady of Fate, if I remember correctly its highly suspected though not quite confirmed. The Lady of Fate is easily the most mysterious of all the major wraiths out there. She predates Charon, directed him to create Stygia, is the nominal leader of the Legion of Fate and her only real appearance in WtO is at its end, where she is the only major NPC to actually survive the events of the scenario. Where Charon and the Deathlords all either Transcend or are destroyed she survives, wordlessly says goodbye to the PCs, who have become the replacements to Charon and the Deathlords, before one of the oldest Ferrymen takes her away to who knows where. Though if I recall there are mentions here and there that she's ultimately waiting for the day when she rejoin her family, the day that's been keeping her going through all the eons.<br /> <br /> *At least a few Deathlords have been replaced over the centuries. The Emerald Lord during WWI was a backstabbing, double-dealing, greedy asshole and was ultimate destroyed by those he betrayed while his modern counterpart is a far, far different individual. Similarly during that same time period there were two Laughing Ladies, the original who had been forced to abdicate by the Smiling Lord and his uprising and her replacement a Smiling Lord supporter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","user":"AkatsukiLeader13","date":". 01-19-2015, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T18:59:11-08:00","id":375766,"title":"","content":"Just a correction.... Charon was originally Mycenaean, not Mesopotamian. That knocks him a millenia or two even further away from the First/Second Cities than being a Mesopotamian... depending on how you slice &quot;Mesopotamian&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T06:27:45-08:00","id":376144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How well known about is Enoch in the various Dark Kingdoms? </div> </div> </div>Enoch is a ghost story among ghosts, a lost city of vampires deep in the Tempest. Most people think it's bullshit, but the Ferrymen and Guildmasters of the Harbingers know better. Enoch's existence is an open secret in the Harbingers, as is the location - but anyone who wants the location of Enoch would be checked for Catharsis immediately, because that's like saying you'd like to jump into the Grand Canyon without a parachute and survive it.<br /> <br /> Stygia occupied Enoch some time after the Third Great Malestrom. The Smiling Lord knows exactly where Stygia is, he's just not strong enough - politically, militarily - to retake it, and Enoch's not <i>that</i> great as a strategic citadel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T07:07:57-08:00","id":376172,"title":"","content":"Re: Eve and the Lady of Fate, in Ends of Empire the Lady tells Erik that she's hoping her son will wind up his affairs soon so she can resolve things with him. Erik asks how old her son is. The Lady says around 9-10,000 years, but only the vampires are really counting any more.<br /> <br /> I remember there being speculation that Abel was Anubis, based on Ends of Empire saying Anubis was spiritually akin to the Lady of Fate, and it being rumoured he was the first man to die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T00:39:29-08:00","id":380846,"title":"","content":"Connection between the Neverborn and the Children is quite a common one to make especially if you consider the Nephandi connection as laid bare in the Book of Madness Revised, and in the second edition as well I have the page numbers for both in another thread, that pretty much places most of the Nephandi Lords, outside of the Malphean Nephandi, as the mere dreams of the Neverborn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T04:02:39-08:00","id":380890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/372242-dead-and-deader-vampire-and-wraith-interaction#post372242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>General:</u></b><br /> <br /> One question I have here is this:<br /> <br /> I can people killed by vampire in connection to necessity, Masquerade or Jyhad as falling under Violence for the purpose of Legion assignment (Smiling Lord right?). However, not every feeding is violent. So I am wondering what Legion those who died from Vampiric exsanguination would fall under? (Fate maybe?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Legion placement is pretty situational. Here are some possibilities, depending on which &quot;angle&quot; you come from...<br /> <br /> -Skeletal Legion (Disease): In life, the wraith suffered from chronic anemia. The vampire feeding on him just made a bad situation worse...<br /> <br /> -Grim Legion (Violence): There was a fight. Maybe he didn't like the way that pale-looking creep was looking at him. Or maybe it was the other way around. Someone got pissed. Someone got dead.<br /> <br /> -Emerald Legion (Happenstance): Maybe he just stumbled on the vampire in a vulnerable moment and saw something he wasn't supposed to see. One must uphold the masquerade. Tough luck.<br /> <br /> -Silent Legion (Despair): He would do anything for his vampire master. Just to feel the rush of the kiss again... his life was in shambles anyway. Might as well go while giving the vampire what he needed... It's not like anyone is going to miss one loser blood doll...<br /> <br /> -Legion of Paupers (Mystery): Last thing I knew, I went to bed with that rockin' redhead... she was kissing my neck and then I woke up here. (Also, when a conflict arises between two of the other legions over who gets someone, they are often given to the Legion of Paupers as a comrpomise.)<br /> <br /> -Legion of Fate (Fate): There must have been some reason, some purpose that led me to that vampire...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/372242-dead-and-deader-vampire-and-wraith-interaction#post372242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you guys think its viable to have a Vampire character take both the Merit and the Flaw and have one represent the Wraith and another the Wraiths Shadow? With the idea that the Wraith in question has trouble keeping his Shadow under control now and then.<br /> <br /> I kinda like the idea of maybe a oneshot or few session game where one PC is the Vampire and one PC is the Wraith and they kinda have a misadventure/plot together. Nice little personal story to be had in that I think. Could be played up for either fun (48 Hours), dark comedy (Withnail and I), slice of life (Being Human) or horror/thriller (Six Sense) depending on the ST and Players mood.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, I can't really talk on the matter of Wraith merits and flaws. I don't know if there is anything similar that might help plant story seeds for interaction between Wraiths and Vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>A wraith's shadow is like a vampire's beast but worse... For one, it talks. It can play tricks on the wraith depending on what &quot;thorns&quot; the wraith has. It plots against the wraith. It only really gets to take control (called catharsis) when the wraith gains a great deal of angst. Also, the shadow is the wraith's foe, first and foremost.<br /> <br /> So in order for the shadow to be represented by your flaw, you have to be pretty strongly tied with the Wraith's goals where the shadow believes that by screwing with you, he screws with the wraith's goals even more.<br /> <br /> Also, there are two sorts of people who can see wraiths without difficulty: The very young and innocent who don't understand death yet, and the insane. Not every madman can see the dead, but the right mental affliction (having to do with death and the dead and the like) can give actual perception of the dead. Malkavian, anyone?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/372242-dead-and-deader-vampire-and-wraith-interaction#post372242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) I was thinking about the idea of a Vampire as a Wraiths fetter in the Skinlands. If that's possible at all (I'm not sure if non-objects can be fetters).</div> </div> </div> </div>Fetters, by necessity, belong to the skinlands. And yes, they can be people, as well as places and objecs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/372242-dead-and-deader-vampire-and-wraith-interaction#post372242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in some ways I guess it sucks. You rely on the Vampire that killed you to stay close to the Skinlands and not get sucked down into the Tempest/Sunless Sea. That's just one more injustice that the universe seems to have thrown at you. Its very likely your not going to like the Vampire in question. Yet it is kinda in your interest to keep him alive and around. This does not mean you can't cause trouble for him of course, so vengeance can be had in small amounts.<br /> <br /> However, the fact your tied to an undead being might be pretty good for you in the long run right? You've got a Fetter that's pretty much immune to mundane aging. So you don't have to worry about him &quot;breaking&quot; like a normal object or dying like a mortal anchor. Vampires are also a fair bit tougher then Humans, so the likelihood of death by accident or mundane violence is a little bit slimmer too. So you could have a way back to being close to the skinlands for centuries or millenia if your lucky.<br /> <br /> I've got no real question here, however, I am very interested in peoples thoughts in regards to this point. Do you think its possible a Wraith starts of resenting their Vampire killer but over time basically grows to kinda accept the fact that their killer is the only thing keeping them close to the world they knew? Maybe even accept that after all the loved ones and friends are dead, their killer is going to be around and forgiveness could actually occur?<br /> <br /> I'll be back later with the more specific points of Vampire that cross-over I feel. For now I must rest and think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. I think the victims of murder often have their murderers as fetters, which presents the wraith with quite a conundrum. Fetters can be resolved, and I believe once a wraith fully resolves a fetter, he is free to occupy the shadowlands ever after, but I would have to consult my book.<br /> <br /> And learning to forgive the vampire, or at least come to an understanding that he stumbled into a tiger's den, whether he realized it or not at the time, and the tiger only did what came naturally to it...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T14:13:40-08:00","id":383573,"title":"","content":"I'm currently working Enoch and the Black Hand into my game. I've had the ridiculous book for almost two decades and I finally decided to use the material. I'm taking inspiration from the destruction of Enoch in Ends of Empire and working my players into the position Eric was through. So far my players discovered Enrathi revenants gathering children for transport as future Chatterlings. The mass grave required for the Level 6 ritual to enter Enoch was mistaken for a sickening attempt at mass murder. While they intervened, the vampire coming to perform the ritual was less than pleased.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3138-old-rusty-pipe","name":"Old Rusty Pipe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T06:08:44-07:00","id":436933,"title":"","content":"Okay, this is a long post...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/372242-dead-and-deader-vampire-and-wraith-interaction?p=374944#post374944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <u><i>Set \u2013</i></u><br /> <br /> So the Gehenna book states he\u2019s physically kicking around the Underworld (though it never explains exactly how he got there, or how he survived the Sixth Great Maelstrom when Cappadocius does not) and waging a conflict with \u201cThe Western Lands\u201d there. One could also ask the question of what he\u2019s feeding off down there, but once again he\u2019s an AntiD, so let\u2019s not dwell on that too much (it\u2019s implied his Lector Priests keep him fed on Setite faith anyway).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Set could be using powers similar to the Nagaraja. That is, if he even retains a physical body. He might be something akin to a mummy (first and second edition, not revised), as their stories are intertwined, or he may at least have used some of the stolen knowledge his side used to create Bane Mummies to give him some kind of possibility of bodily resurrection.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/372242-dead-and-deader-vampire-and-wraith-interaction?p=374944#post374944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <u><i>Arikel \u2013</i></u><br /> <br /> ...another name she goes by is Ishtar, famous for travelling to the Underworld and trying to get a loved one back to the land of the living. <br /> <br /> ...So she could be a mover and shaker in any one of the Dark Kingdoms (though Stygia is most likely\u2026not including Enoch of course, if we consider her Wraith/Specter as a possible member of the Aralu) under another name.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>She could be one of the Aralu, yes. One did have that name in <i>Dirty Secrets</i> (there were four or five Aralu, and Inauhaten said one was Arikel; others think Loz could be Toreador). This ties into the possibility I outline below for Ventru.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/372242-dead-and-deader-vampire-and-wraith-interaction?p=374944#post374944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <u><i>Ventru \u2013</i></u><br /> <br /> Unlike Arikel, the cannon version of Ventru\u2019s story has him die (by Troiles hand) outside the gates of the Second City shortly before the city fell. Some evidence exists that he planned his own death and might have even be suicidal. So like the non-cannon Arikel, there is a descent candidate for him to become a Wraith.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Likewise, Ventru could also be one of the Aralu. <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Aralu\" target=\"_blank\">It's implied one of those beings might be Ventru (Nergal)</a>. If you prefer to ignore other cosomologies, then the Aralu may be the wraithly embodiments (or whatever lingers after the 'death') of Antediluvians. <br /> <br /> However, Ambrogino Giovanni saw angelic beings evacuating the city upon its destruction. It's hinted in the <i>Hunter ST's Companion </i>(and this fits with what Ambrogino saw) that the three Aralu/angelic figures seen leaving Enoch might be the Messengers who give the Imbued (Hunters) their power. If there were indeed five Aralu (legends vary from three to five), then the other two Aralu could be the Ministers themselves, who are the masters of the Messengers (the Scarlet Empress and Ebon Dragon who also empowered the Kuei-jin in past ages).<br /> <br /> All this is particularly interesting, though, because <i>Gehenna</i> specifically states that the Scarlet Empress is a facet of Lilith (who has become elevated to the level of a god/Celestial Incarna, equal to Lucifer and Yahweh), who is also a ruler of the Dragon-Blooded (precursors of the Kuei-jin in early plans for the game) in <i>Exalted</i>. Some consider the Ebon Dragon to be Caine (KotE lore), however that's less certain, as Lilith and he part ways in most sources. <i>Giovanni Chronicles I</i> does suggest that Lilith and Yahweh are the dark and light halves of a Godhead, however, which might imply Yahweh was the Ebon Dragon instead (or 'dragon' could refer to Lucifer or even another aspect of Lilith). In this version of reality, it implies Celestial Incarna/gods take different forms for different cosmologies and depending on whoever's viewing them (e.g., Yahweh is also the August Personage of Jade). This fits with the subjective reality concept in mage, and the mention of Creation actually existing on various levels of literal and metaphorical existence in <i>Demon</i>, making many of the conflicting myths all true at the same time to a degree. It could also be true that with each new age of man, the consensus reshuffles a little bit, so that reality reshapes itself retrospectively and the truth evolves/changes, creating inconsistencies in mapping out any objective cosmology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/372242-dead-and-deader-vampire-and-wraith-interaction?p=374944#post374944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <u><i>Abel \u2013</i></u><br /> <br /> He\u2019s the first human to ever die and the first murder victim. It seems pretty thematically appropriate that he becomes a Wraith to me. Hell, he\u2019d technically be the first Wraith.<br /> One Gehenna scenario even has the PC\u2019s call up Abel as a Ghost to confront Caine. So it seems to fit that he\u2019s still around and not Shadow-Eaten by the modern nights.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Abel, or at least the memory of him, is kept in one of Oblivion's Memory Towers. So he's already accounted for, and is separate to Charon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/372242-dead-and-deader-vampire-and-wraith-interaction?p=374944#post374944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alternatively, a nice little twist could be that he did become Shadow-Eaten and his Shadow started off the whole manifestation of Oblivion in the Underworld. Maybe he\u2019s now a stupidly powerful Onceborn or even the entity sitting at the heart of the Void.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If Abel is imprisoned within one of Oblivion's memory towers, it could imply that he is the buried Psyche of Oblivion, and Oblivion is his Shadow. However, the Grand Maw/Grandma (Oblivion's 'consciousness') is basically a giant symbol of the Monstrous Feminine (in critical theory, the devouring, Freudian vagina symbolising the threat of the mother who threatens to swallow the feeble-minded man-child who is terrified of such things). She sounds more like a <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Primordials\" target=\"_blank\">Primordial</a> than anything else (like Malfeas, or Autochthon, or Gaia), and could be either <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Cytherea\" target=\"_blank\">Cytherea</a> or a similar generative being who died and therefore took on a new, corrupted purpose. Alternatively, she could simply be an aspect of the Wyrm (the aspect trapped by the Weaver and driven mad, known as the Wyrm of Balance).<br /> <br /> <i>Orpheus</i> implies she could be God's dark twin, but the dark twin of Gaia would be more likely. It's implied in <i>Orpheus</i> that Oblivion is a fundamental paradox, and hides its own paradoxical nature in its memory towers (Abel, who conversely connects Oblivion to all of life itself). It might be that Oblivion is the dark twin of the universe itself, and the embodiment of the paradox of Creation emerging from Nothingness. Or, going right back to the Wraith core book and forgetting everything else, Oblivion could simply be the pain of the universe when the Neverborn were killed. It wishes to create (as revealed in <i>Orpheus: End Game</i>) in a strange way, but not because it is a generative being in itself. Rather, it seeks out creation (with a small 'c') because it is inextricably tied to Creation (with a big 'C'). Its duty is to destroy, so that Creation might create anew and thus give it more things to destroy again, with each half of that reality feeding the other (Creation to Oblivion, Oblivion to Creation). Creation and Oblivion could, in effect, be the ouroboros, with the destructive head (Oblivion) gorging on the generative tail (Creation), but the generative tail also emerging from the destructive head.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/372242-dead-and-deader-vampire-and-wraith-interaction?p=374944#post374944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So the Neverborn in Wraith are entities that predate our realities existence. Existing in this reality is torment to them and they hate every aspect of our reality. They want everything to cease so that they can go back to non-existence (as we understand it) which seems to be their natural habitat. If they ever woke up they would pretty much start demolishing our reality in short order. Luckily they spend most of their time asleep because the Underworld, while less painful to them then the living one, kinda dopes them up a fair bit.<br /> <br /> So the Children from Clanbook Baali are entities that predate our realities existence. Existing in this reality is torment to them and they hate every aspect of our reality. They want everything to cease so that they can go back to non-existence (as we understand it) which seems to be their natural habitat. If they ever woke up they would pretty much start demolishing our reality in short order. Luckily the Baali use atrocities and the \u201cbreaking\u201d of their True names to keep them asleep in the hidden and deep \u201cplaces\u201d of the living material world.<br /> <br /> Hang on a second\u2026<br /> <br /> If we tie this in with the story at the start of the Baali Clanbook that some of the Children burned up and died when God created the light at the start of time, well, it seems the Neverborn might be \u201cdead\u201d (I use this term loosely, I don\u2019t thinking something that pre-dates our reality can really die as we understand the concept at least) Children.<br /> <br /> Anybody else had this thought? Anyone come up with other possible links between Vampire stuff and the Neverborn?</div> </div> </div> </div>In <i>Exalted</i>, the Neverborn are dead Primordials, whose undying nature meant the Underworld was created when they were 'slain' by the gods/Celestial Incarna (an act which ruptured Creation because of the paradox of killing beings who can't die). Their living siblings were <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Malfeas_(AOS)\" target=\"_blank\">imprisoned in the body of Malfeas</a> (another Primordial) and became the Yozi (probably the masters (Urge Wyrms?) of the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Malfeas_(cWOD)\" target=\"_blank\">Maeljin Incarna</a>/<a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Infernal_Exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Exalted</a> of the oWoD/<i>Exalted</i>). As Malfeas exists in both <i>Mage</i> and <i>Werewolf</i>, we might assume the two realms are the same in both the oWoD and <i>Exalted</i>. In which case, the Children might be any Primordial (Yozi or Neverborn) which the Baali can contact.<br /> <br /> However, <i>Demon: The Fallen</i> and later VtM supplements later confused matters, by implying the Children were simply Earthbound (and tying the Earthbound into a Judeo-Christian context). This perspective might be considered biased, of course, as the angels and demons were all creations of Yahweh, which means they would recognise his worldview, rather than the more polytheistic one implied by other games (in which Yahweh is just one of the Celestial Incarna, albeit their presumed ruler in the West, who collectively seized power from the Primordials before them). The Earthbound could merely have opted to become the servants of the Primordials, which would allow both options to be true.<br /> <br /> Wow! This post was longer than I thought...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T10:11:42-07:00","id":437159,"title":"","content":"I seem to recall reading something in DtF that implied the Hell of that gameline was the same thing as the Labyrinth in Wraith, and that wraiths became spectres when they were caught by demons and sucked down into Hell for a time before being regurgitated back up into the Shadowlands (making the demons analogous to the Neverborn, I guesss).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T11:12:23-07:00","id":437270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/372242-dead-and-deader-vampire-and-wraith-interaction?p=437159#post437159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem to recall reading something in DtF that implied the Hell of that gameline was the same thing as the Labyrinth in Wraith, and that wraiths became spectres when they were caught by demons and sucked down into Hell for a time before being regurgitated back up into the Shadowlands (making the demons analogous to the Neverborn, I guesss).</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons come from the Abyss, which is apparently beneath Oblivion (the Tempest is above Oblivion). They're probably separate realms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T22:52:20-07:00","id":438077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/372242-dead-and-deader-vampire-and-wraith-interaction?p=437270#post437270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Demons come from the Abyss, which is apparently beneath Oblivion (the Tempest is above Oblivion). They're probably separate realms.</div> </div> </div> </div>DtF posited that the Demons could hear the wailing of human souls through the walls of their prison making Abyss most likely be either in the Tempest or tacked on to hte Labyrinth with at least one wall so to speak against Tempest.<br /> <br /> Besides there is nothing beneath Oblivion as it is the end point. Of everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T05:24:25-07:00","id":438289,"title":"","content":"Tha Abyss is usually described as being 'beneath' the Underworld: <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Abyss_(DTF\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Abyss_(DTF</a>). That's a rather vague/metaphorical description, however, and probably not exclusively geographical. But I do recall reading it was below Oblivion specifically, although I'll have to have a think where I thought I saw that. As the Elohim built reality (including, presumably, Oblivion), they're probably not fettered by its physical bounds. Besides, the Abyss sounds like the primal darkness/nothingness before God and Creation, so it could very easily be beyond the bounds of the world described in the games. Oblivion, it seems, is very much a part of Creation (see Orpheus).<br /> <br /> While the Fallen can hear the wails of the dead, they can also hear human suffering generally, as I understood it. So they may not even need to be physically proximate to any other part of Creation to hear this. God might have the sounds piped in from elsewhere in the universe to make a kind of torturous muzak.<br /> <br /> However, the Fallen's imprisonment also sounds similar to that of the Maeljin Incarna, who are in Malfeas. Malfeas contains the Black Spiral, which allegedly connects to the Labyrinth. The Abyss and Malfeas could be the same or similar, with it actually being a pocket reality (like the various Yomi Worlds) within the greater cosmos, and with one or more routes to other parts of Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 03-12-2015, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T06:05:27-07:00","id":438309,"title":"","content":"First of all Orpheus should not be taken as Wraith Canon, what parts of it should will be revealed in their writeup in Wraith 20th, as it mangled and mutilated pretty much everything established in Wraith. Including the role of the Neverborn and the Oblivion as you pointed out. Not a single Wraith source, or any other besides Orpheus which was kinda it's own thing outside and parallel to cWoD in general I always felt it was a standalone game that used similar mechanics and that was all, gives such attributes to Oblivion, or even any kind of actual sentience as it is mostly described as a universal constant that is growing slowly as it readies to end all things. The whole Grandmaw thing has no bearing in Wraith.<br /> <br /> Demon was notorious in how it ignored and mangled other lines metaphysics, the Elohim supposedly created everything yet had no knowledge of or way to interact with the Umbra, Charon and Nhudri both were labeled as their number etc. But the fact remains that if you read through the DtF books you'll see that the Elohim also somehow in their creation of the underworld failed to actually notice the presence of the Neverborn amongst other things it is not too far fetched that their actual bearings in there might be a bit scrambled. Any way I did write of this art length some time a go, nor sure if it was this incarnation of the forum or the previous one, so you might find that floating around somewhere it had book quotes and such which I am too tied up for time to get now, not to mention too lazy, but I am quite confident that the Elohims prison realm Abyss was located somewhere close to the Labyrinth, even perhaps attached to it, and against the Tempest. Also do note that from the Elohims perspective Tempest itself is below the underworld proper and Labyrinth is far below that.<br /> <br /> The realms outside of Creation proper are to be found if one travels far enough in to the Umbra leaving our solar system and more behind. That is also the realm where the Dream of the Neverborn are manifest as the Outsider Masters of the K'llashaa.<br /> <br /> Black Spiral Labyrinth has never been directly linked to Oblivion per se, there is a sidebar that describes the difference between Oblivion and Wyrm and the links in between, found in a Wraith book cannot remember which though possibly Buried Secrets or Wraith Players Guide my memory isn't what it used to be, but if I recall correctly the difference is that the Oblivion is a passive force of destruction from which nothing returns whole the Wyrm is an active force of destruction and entropy but that from it's destruction new things may spring. Wyrms destruction is part of the cycle of Wylds Creation, Weavers Stability and Wyrms destruction of the excess and return to the cycle while things that fall into Oblivion cease to be it literally is the end of everything. Even the Neverborn who are finally returned to their original non-existant state.<br /> <br /> Exalted as a line makes great assumptions that would change especially the origins of the Neverborn, and Oblivion as well though Oblivions purpose would remain the same, but that line has long since been officially untangled from both of the WoDs. So it's Canon should not be taken as Canon past of any of the existing WoD lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T08:36:33-07:00","id":438440,"title":"","content":"Well the OP is specially talking about crossover games, so bringing in other games lines is kind of the point. You can keep the mythologies separate if you wish, of course, but this thread was started with a question exploring the tangles that occur when the gamelines are brought together. This post continues in that vein (seeking interconnections, even if they're, well, in vain).<br /> <br /> Having the Black Spiral directly connected to the Labyrinth (via a spiritual pathway) doesn't mean the Wyrm and Oblivion have to be one and the same. Yomi Wan has pathways leading to and from all sorts of other worlds. I think you thought I meant 'connected' as in 'the same' or 'spiritually related'. I'm referring to routes like trods or dragon lines or byways. That doesn't necessary imply any of these interconnected things have an objective existential/causal relationship.<br /> <br /> However, back to the idea of crossovers, while the Wyrm is active and Oblivion is passive, you could go the Yang/Yin route of KotE and interpret them as both being the Yang and Yin aspects of the part of the Wheel that destroys/recycles. Not the same thing, but mirroring each other in an active/passive binary. The oWoD is full of such dualities, so it's really not a huge leap of faith. Again, this isn't explicit in the material, but we're supposing again for the sake of crossovers.<br /> <br /> The parallels between Exalted and the oWoD, on the other hand, are just useful for helping to conceptualise some of the ideas. Neverborn claim they either came into existence at the moment the Underworld was created, or predate Yahweh's Creation altogether. Exalted has both as true (if you see Yahweh as semi-analagous to the Unconquered Sun). I know it's an act in futility, but so long as the correspondences between the two settings exist, there will always be some relationship inferred by players. I personally find it fun, but I know others hate linking the two.<br /> <br /> Back to 'outside of Creation'--I meant beyond even the Umbra (which has a form). Literally the darkness before God said 'Let there be light.' I'll explain why I mention this in a minute. There's constant reference to this nothingness or darkness in various gamelines (it's the place the Children apparently fell from and one possible origin of the Malfeans, for example). This darkness is the antithesis of Creation and the absence of God. In a Gnostic sense, it is everything outside the world of the Artificer God, or the shadow simultaneously created by the light of what the Artificer built, and perhaps even the Divine Reality (less likely). In a Greek paradigm, it could be the world of the Titans (Primordials) who existed before the Olympians (gods). Thus those who are banished from God's presence, or receive 'The Anathema of the One' as it's been described (in the Guarded Rubrics), are creatures of darkness that often can't bear the light (Caine, Lilith, the Children). Demons can bear the light, but are literally denied it while in the Abyss. <br /> <br /> The Abyss could, of course, be in the Labyrinth in the DtF cosmology. It's probably the gameline I know least, and as you say, it seemed to contradict so much of the earlier source material (although each game does, to a degree). I have heard that theory before (it might even have been the post of yours you're talking about). The implications of it being in or adjacent to the Abyss, however, are certainly interesting from a wraith perspective--particularly now there are cracks. Can you imagine battling escaped demons as well as spectres? And some of these greater demons must surely be able to command the spectres? (On a side note, re: demons having little grasp of the Underworld, I'd always seen them like deluded golems of Yahweh, believing his strict interpretation of reality, whether it was true or not.)<br /> <br /> An idea that occurred to me (again, not necessarily a likely one, but one a Storyteller with a crossover campaign might be interested in) is that perhaps Grandma wasn't Oblivion, after all, but a demon who, for whatever reason, had occupied Oblivion. We know the Earthbound inhabit locations because they don't have bodies (in this sense they're very similar to Primordials like Gaia, who are a location or realm in themselves), so if we see the Grand Maw equally as a location (the lip or event horizon of a black hole, in effect) then that could be a possibility.<br /> <br /> Getting deeper into abstract philosophical points, Grandma could even be the native nothingness from which Yahweh and Creation actually came in the first place (she's motherly, sort of), as things definitely spew from the Well of the Void (such as maelstroms). Gnosticism has Sophia as the mother of Yahweh, and she represents a kind of primordial knowledge. Again, I find these possibilities intriguing. Anyway, sorry, I'm getting waaaay too much into abstractions here... We got off-topic about vampires and wraiths, didn't we? :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T10:22:57-07:00","id":438656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/372242-dead-and-deader-vampire-and-wraith-interaction?p=438440#post438440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> An idea that occurred to me (again, not necessarily a likely one, but one a Storyteller with a crossover campaign might be interested in) is that perhaps Grandma wasn't Oblivion, after all, but a demon who, for whatever reason, had occupied Oblivion. We know the Earthbound inhabit locations because they don't have bodies (in this sense they're very similar to Primordials like Gaia, who are a location or realm in themselves), so if we see the Grand Maw equally as a location (the lip or event horizon of a black hole, in effect) then that could be a possibility.<br /> <br /> Getting deeper into abstract philosophical points, Grandma could even be the native nothingness from which Yahweh and Creation actually came in the first place (she's motherly, sort of), as things definitely spew from the Well of the Void (such as maelstroms). Gnosticism has Sophia as the mother of Yahweh, and she represents a kind of primordial knowledge. Again, I find these possibilities intriguing. Anyway, sorry, I'm getting waaaay too much into abstractions here... We got off-topic about vampires and wraiths, didn't we? :P</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are looking for Grandmaw to be a Earthbound, you have to figure out who summoned her out of the Abyss and how that entity got ahold of the rituals Lucifer created to free his lieutenants. Demons don't escape the Abyss until the Seals are broken without being summoned to Earth... or the Labyrinth in this case.<br /> <br /> One of the alternative presentations of Grandmaw certainly seems like she has something to do with the darkness &amp; deep that Yawheh looked out on before he started talking about this &quot;light&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> Neither of those things is impossible, just require some more explanation. And they aren't mutually exclusive either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T10:43:20-07:00","id":438676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/372242-dead-and-deader-vampire-and-wraith-interaction?p=438309#post438309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Demon was notorious in how it ignored and mangled other lines metaphysics, the Elohim supposedly created everything yet had no knowledge of or way to interact with the Umbra, Charon and Nhudri both were labeled as their number etc. But the fact remains that if you read through the DtF books you'll see that the Elohim also somehow in their creation of the underworld failed to actually notice the presence of the Neverborn amongst other things it is not too far fetched that their actual bearings in there might be a bit scrambled. Any way I did write of this art length some time a go, nor sure if it was this incarnation of the forum or the previous one, so you might find that floating around somewhere it had book quotes and such which I am too tied up for time to get now, not to mention too lazy, but I am quite confident that the Elohims prison realm Abyss was located somewhere close to the Labyrinth, even perhaps attached to it, and against the Tempest. Also do note that from the Elohims perspective Tempest itself is below the underworld proper and Labyrinth is far below that.</div> </div> </div> </div>They may not be as mangled as they seem. There are some direct references to the fact that the world the demons return to is &quot;broken&quot; and their descriptions of the world before their imprisonment is one in which the Umbra and the current physical were one and the same. Spirits were the things they now represent. That's an idea that gets some traction in Werewolf as well. Demons aren't interacting with the Umbra because it is going to have to be brought to their attention that it exists, since they are just seeing a world that is sadly lacking in certain inherent ways. It doesn't immediately follow that if you find something broken, you would assume that the missing bits are just somewhere else &quot;re-assembled&quot; as some new thing that is adjacent and touching the remainder but no longer integral and continuous. Why can't they affect it very well? Because it's not really something they are equipped to deal with. It just didn't exist in anything remotely resembling its current form when they were busy building everything. <br /> <br /> Nhudri got sucked up into DtF as a Fallen Angel, but it seems like an okay extrapolation as his origins are deliberately mysterious in Wraith. If you don't want crossover, then Nhudri is a mystery with a different solution. So DtF has him as a Malefactor (I think?) that somehow escaped the Abyss (How? I can't remember if that was addressed.) and was lost and imprisoned in the Labyrinth until Charon found him and rescued him. It specifically mentions that Charon was the name of one of the greatest of the Halaku/Reapers and that when the Demons broke free and heard he was running the Underworld, they got excited and tried to track him down only to discover that he was almost certainly just some old wraith who had taken Charon's name as his own. Similarly the Reapers may not have noticed the Neverborn as ALL of the Elohim are born after the &quot;Fiat lux&quot; moment when Creation commenced. So, post the darkness in which the Neverborn sport. It's an extrapolation, but even the &quot;dark&quot; of the Underworld may not quite reach the &quot;primal&quot; dark that preceded the start of Creation. Also, we know there were other places the Elohim didn't have a clue about. They were completely and unhappily surprised by the existence of the Abyss. It's kinda like having the Halaku build a house (the Underworld) right on top of a bank vault (the Abyss) and a sinkhole (Oblivion). And the Neverborn were crawling around in the dirt of the foundation, below the Underworld and above the Abyss. If such 3-D terms really pertain in discussions of such topological complexity. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T11:34:11-07:00","id":438725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Back to 'outside of Creation'--I meant beyond even the Umbra (which has a form). Literally the darkness before God said 'Let there be light.' I'll explain why I mention this in a minute. There's constant reference to this nothingness or darkness in various gamelines (it's the place the Children apparently fell from and one possible origin of the Malfeans, for example). This darkness is the antithesis of Creation and the absence of God. In a Gnostic sense, it is everything outside the world of the Artificer God, or the shadow simultaneously created by the light of what the Artificer built, and perhaps even the Divine Reality (less likely). </div> </div> </div>Thgis is the very same outside of Creation I was talking about. The place from which the K'llashaa Masters come from, far beyond the Horizon in the Umbra, is in several places described as being outside of Creation which is why they are so Paradoxical to our Creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They were completely and unhappily surprised by the existence of the Abyss. It's kinda like having the Halaku build a house (the Underworld) right on top of a bank vault (the Abyss) and a sinkhole (Oblivion). And the Neverborn were crawling around in the dirt of the foundation, below the Underworld and above the Abyss. If such 3-D terms really pertain in discussions of such topological complexity. </div> </div> </div>I have laughed this same concept in another thread, how clueless they were burrowing their &quot;Haven&quot; right there aside the beings that pre-existed Creation itself and hated it with all their non-being.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the world before their imprisonment is one in which the Umbra and the current physical were one and the same. Spirits were the things they now represent. That's an idea that gets some traction in Werewolf as well. Demons aren't interacting with the Umbra because it is going to have to be brought to their attention that it exists, since they are just seeing a world that is sadly lacking in certain inherent ways. </div> </div> </div>I think I posited this same thing last time someone asked for crossover help with Demon in one of the several &quot;questions about DtF&quot; threads that were popping up here a while ago.<br /> <br /> But the fact that we can force these things to be, like the existence of the Umbra, in DtF doesn't actually correct the fact htey kinda forgot about a whole realm of existence when designing the game. Like I've said several times in several threads Devil's Due is generally a better version of Demon to use in Crossover games mechanically and otherwise, in fact it is generally a better version of DtF but naturally YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T14:47:13-07:00","id":438904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/372242-dead-and-deader-vampire-and-wraith-interaction?p=438725#post438725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thgis is the very same outside of Creation I was talking about. The place from which the K'llashaa Masters come from, far beyond the Horizon in the Umbra, is in several places described as being outside of Creation which is why they are so Paradoxical to our Creation.<br /> <br /> <br /> I have laughed this same concept in another thread, how clueless they were burrowing their &quot;Haven&quot; right there aside the beings that pre-existed Creation itself and hated it with all their non-being.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think I posited this same thing last time someone asked for crossover help with Demon in one of the several &quot;questions about DtF&quot; threads that were popping up here a while ago.<br /> <br /> But the fact that we can force these things to be, like the existence of the Umbra, in DtF doesn't actually correct the fact htey kinda forgot about a whole realm of existence when designing the game. Like I've said several times in several threads Devil's Due is generally a better version of Demon to use in Crossover games mechanically and otherwise, in fact it is generally a better version of DtF but naturally YMMV.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps they forgot about it. Perhaps not. It may have been tagged &quot;to be handled later&quot;. It certainly ended up in the associated fiction where the demon laments the broken state of the world, remembering when coffee was a plant, a refreshing drink and a helpful spirit all at the same time or when on of the fallen posited that, when the angels fell, the world fell too, cracking apart, and it was that the hand of God that caught it and held it together, not as it was, but as something changed. In essence, I guess, kinda like having something knocked out of your hand and simultaneously fixing it while catching it. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, maybe they just ditched the Umbra with only the occasional nod to irk the crossover type. I mean, c'mon.... how could the Earthbound not started mucking around with the Umbra? They had thousands of years and developed tons of other powers....<br /> <br /> If the Halaku were the contractors, it's hard to blame them for bad placement.... Whomever (or WHOMever to King James it up) was responsible for site selection and zoning was more at fault. Maybe that's the place the Underworld HAD to be built for some kind of transphysical resonance reasons. (Which would make a zoning issue.)<br /> <br /> Perhaps the Neverborn are just the Cthulhoid entities, I mean, K'LLASHAA MASTERS, that didn't sit there at the edge of Oblivion, Abyss-adajcent,marinating in Underworldly juices for the duration of the universe. And the K'llashaa are Neverbone that just sat out there becoming stranger and stranger by means of some reverse induction. Be being near reality but not off it or in it, they become less and less like that which is reality....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T02:29:41-07:00","id":441117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/372242-dead-and-deader-vampire-and-wraith-interaction?p=438440#post438440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the OP is specially talking about crossover games, so bringing in other games lines is kind of the point. You can keep the mythologies separate if you wish, of course, but this thread was started with a question exploring the tangles that occur when the gamelines are brought together. This post continues in that vein (seeking interconnections, even if they're, well, in vain).</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair. I kinda stated my mission statement at the start of this thread. Namely that I was going to run a game that used V20/V20DA, M20 and Wr20 as the only games/setting/metaphysics involved. As I mentioned previously, I was thinking of using KOTE as well, but that would be a later inclusion IF it gets the X20 treatment and gets revised. <br /> <br /> While theorising about stuff from Werewolf, Changeling,Hunter, Mummy, Demon and Orpheus is cool, it not really something that I was thinking of using any elements of. Werewolves in my game are going to be the Lupines out of V20 (with maybe an infernal sub-type that is going to be introduced in V20DA Book of Secrets). Demons are more in line with how Vampire and Mage treat them, namely horrible entities that seem to dwell in hell, are interested in souls and corrupt everything they touch. Hunters are Hunters Hunted style underdogs, some of which have lesser supernatural abilities like Theurgy or Numina to help them out. Mummy's don't exist. Changelings stopped existing in the Dark Ages. Orpheus will likely get the bits that are going to be in Wr20 used and everything else ignored.<br /> <br /> As for the Exalted inclusion. I've never read that game line. Though I am going to get hold of a pdf of the new 3rd Edition when it comes out to see what I think of it. I understand it originally had a rough link to the CWoD back in Exalteds 1st Edition and the CWoD 2nd Edition but both worlds have been separate for some time. Personally, form what I do know about Exalted from internet scanning on it, I think I like it more as its own setting completely removed from any link to the CWoD.<br /> <br /> Not to say I don't find your theorising interesting adambeyoncelowe, just that I was looking for people to critic my ideas/answer my questions/spitball alternate ideas at me from a purely Vampire/Mage/Wraith background. As it's in general a lot more useful to me when it comes to coming up with ideas I might be able to implement in the game setting I'm constructing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T04:36:16-07:00","id":441187,"title":"","content":"Sure. I admitted I got off-topic. However some of the correspondences are quite interesting (for me) and create good fodder for Storytellers. Whenever I do a crossover, I either use the rules from the antagonists section of the core book I'm using or go the whole hog and make everything as it is in its own gameline. YMMV of course, so take what you need and ignore the rest <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> I'm just interested in mapping out the cosmologies in general. I geek out over that stuff. But hopefully some of this stuff has been useful for you anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}